From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:02:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: do not let one interval after idle
 open the swap_pace gate

swap_pace holds an internal-panel frame for the 120 Hz grid only while
the smoothed interval between swap completions is at least
swap_pace_min_us (14.6 ms), i.e. at video rates. An idle gap of 50 ms or
more resets the average, and the first interval after it then seeds the
average alone.

A window that opens after idle often completes one frame, then its first
animation frame 15 to 50 ms later, then frames at 120 Hz. Seeded with
that one gap, the average stays above 14.6 ms for the next eight or so
120 Hz frames (1/8 weight), so they are held for the grid as if they
were video: a terminal opened after 1.5 s idle had 9 of its swaps held
or gated on some runs and none on others, depending on whether that gap
fell below or above 50 ms.

Seed the average with the second interval after an idle gap instead.
Steady video is unchanged; video that starts after a pause is held from
its third frame instead of its second.

Fixes: 4110184c742b ("drm/apple: m4: do not hold the first J604 panel frames after idle")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 23 ++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 6274845002..0550cebc06 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -1811,21 +1811,26 @@ static void dcp_m4_pace_learn(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 
 	if (r->int_prev_done && done > r->int_prev_done) {
 		/*
-		 * An idle gap (50 ms or more) starts the average afresh, so the
-		 * first interval after it decides alone whether video follows.
+		 * An idle gap (50 ms or more) starts the average afresh.
 		 * Counted as 50 ms, it took the first six or so frames of any
 		 * burst after idle (a keystroke, a window opening) for video, and
-		 * they were held for the grid.
+		 * they were held for the grid. Nor does the first interval after
+		 * it seed the average alone: a window that opens often completes
+		 * one frame, then its first animation frame 15 to 50 ms later,
+		 * then frames at 120 Hz, and an average seeded with that one gap
+		 * took the next eight or so for video. The second interval
+		 * seeds it; video is then held from its third frame.
 		 */
 		u64 iv = done - r->int_prev_done;
+		u64 idle = div_u64(arch_timer_get_cntfrq(), 20);
 
-		if (iv >= div_u64(arch_timer_get_cntfrq(), 20))
+		if (iv >= idle)
 			WRITE_ONCE(r->int_iv_ewma, 0);
-		else
-			WRITE_ONCE(r->int_iv_ewma,
-				   r->int_iv_ewma ? (r->int_iv_ewma * 7 + iv) / 8 : iv);
-		WRITE_ONCE(r->int_last_iv,
-			   iv < div_u64(arch_timer_get_cntfrq(), 20) ? iv : 0);
+		else if (r->int_iv_ewma)
+			WRITE_ONCE(r->int_iv_ewma, (r->int_iv_ewma * 7 + iv) / 8);
+		else if (r->int_last_iv)
+			WRITE_ONCE(r->int_iv_ewma, iv);
+		WRITE_ONCE(r->int_last_iv, iv < idle ? iv : 0);
 	}
 	r->int_prev_done = done;
 	if (e) {
